# CLOG keeper environment - copy to .env (not committed, see .gitignore) or
# set these directly in the systemd unit's EnvironmentFile. NONE of this
# file's real, filled-in values ever belong in git - see README.md's
# "Security assumptions" section.

# ── The dedicated keeper EOA's private key ──────────────────────────────────
# REQUIRED. Generate a FRESH keypair for this purpose alone - NEVER the
# deployer, Safe, or governance private key (see README.md for why: every
# action this keeper takes is permissionless by contract design, so this
# key needs no elevated permission whatsoever, and using a privileged key
# here would be a pure, unnecessary loss risk). This key only ever needs
# enough ETH for gas on Robinhood Chain and Arbitrum One - see README.md's
# "Required keeper balances" section for concrete amounts.
KEEPER_PRIVATE_KEY=

# ── RPC endpoints (optional - both have sane public defaults) ──────────────
# ROBINHOOD_RPC_URL=https://rpc.mainnet.chain.robinhood.com
# ARBITRUM_RPC_URL=https://arb1.arbitrum.io/rpc

# ── Operational tuning (optional - all have defaults, see src/config.ts) ───
# How often the decision loop runs, in milliseconds.
# KEEPER_POLL_INTERVAL_MS=30000

# Maximum blocks per eth_getLogs call, for every historical/incremental
# log scan (TokenWatchlist, RoundLedger) - see src/blockRangeChunker.ts.
# Real RPC providers vary in what block range/log count they accept in
# one call; lower this if a specific provider needs a smaller window.
# Default: 2000.
# KEEPER_LOG_CHUNK_BLOCKS=2000

# Below this ETH balance (wei), fundingHealth logs a WARNING for the given
# address. Default: 5000000000000000 (0.005 ETH).
# KEEPER_LOW_BALANCE_WARNING_WEI=5000000000000000

# Where the idempotency lock file lives. Default: keeper/.keeper-lock.json
# (next to this directory, NOT inside dist/ or src/, so it survives a
# rebuild).
# KEEPER_LOCK_FILE=/var/lib/clog-keeper/.keeper-lock.json

# Set to "true" to exit after exactly one pass instead of looping forever -
# --dry-run already implies this; this variable exists for a real (non-dry-
# run) single pass, e.g. for manual/cron-style invocation instead of the
# systemd long-running service.
# KEEPER_RUN_ONCE=false

# ── What is NEVER an env var here ───────────────────────────────────────────
# Contract addresses, chain id, and the deployment block are NOT
# configured here - they come from the tracked deployment manifest,
# ../deployments/robinhood-mainnet.json, the same one the frontend uses.
# See README.md and ../docs/DEPLOYMENTS.md.
